---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RankLadder from "../../components/RankLadder.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config";
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" canonicalPath="/en/" title="Your LoL rank on Discord" description="Moon Poro is the bot of the League of Legends PL Discord server. Sign in with Riot and get roles with your region and Solo/Duo rank.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>Show your rank on the server</h1>
      <p class="lead">Moon Poro is the bot of the League of Legends PL server. Sign in with Riot and the bot gives you roles with your region and Solo/Duo rank. After that, it keeps your rank up to date.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href={siteConfig.discordInviteUrl}>Join the server</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="#how">How to verify</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <RankLadder caption="Every rank has its role. If you're not ranked in Solo/Duo yet, you get the Unranked role." />
  </section>

  <section class="section steps-section" id="how">
    <h2>How to verify</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="phase phase-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Click “Zweryfikuj konto”</h3>
        <p>That's “Verify account”, under the verification panel on the server. The bot sends you a private link.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="phase phase-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Open the link</h3>
        <p>Click “Zaloguj się przez Riot” (“Sign in with Riot”), check that the page shows your Discord account, then click “Przejdź do logowania Riot” (“Go to Riot sign-in”). The link works once, for 10 minutes.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="phase phase-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Sign in to your Riot account</h3>
        <p>You sign in on the Riot Games website with the same account you play on. Riot shares your Riot ID and region with us.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="phase phase-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Done</h3>
        <p>Go back to Discord. Below the message with the link you'll see a confirmation with your Riot ID, region and rank. You now have the “Zweryfikowany” (Verified) and “Użytkownik” (Member) roles plus region and rank roles. If Riot isn't responding right then, the bot adds the rank role a bit later.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section features-section">
    <h2>After verifying</h2>
    <ul class="features">
      <li>
        <p class="feature-key"><span class="discord-button grey">Moje konto</span> <span class="or">or</span> <code>/profil</code></p>
        <p>“My account” shows your linked Riot account, rank, LP and win/loss record. Only you can see it.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="feature-key"><span class="discord-button blurple">Odśwież rangę</span></p>
        <p>Your rank refreshes on its own. After a promotion you don't have to wait: click “Odśwież rangę” (“Refresh rank”). You can do this once every 30 minutes.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p class="feature-key"><span class="discord-button red">Usuń powiązanie</span> <span class="or">or</span> <code>/usun_weryfikacje</code></p>
        <p>“Remove link” disconnects your Riot account and removes the Verified role. Region and rank roles stay.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="band-inner">
      <img src="/moon-poro.png" alt="" width="104" height="104" />
      <div>
        <h2>Your password goes to Riot only</h2>
        <p>You sign in on riotgames.com. Moon Poro never sees your password, and the bot will never ask for it on Discord. Poros prefer Poro-Snax. If someone asks for your password “on behalf of Moon Poro”, it's a scam. Report it to the moderators.</p>
        <p>The link from the bot is only for you. Don't pass it on, and don't open verification links from other people: you would link your Riot account to someone else's Discord.</p>
        <p>For roles we store your Discord account ID, Riot ID, region and rank. Details are in the <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-section">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>The link doesn't work or has expired</summary>
        <p>Each link works once, for 10 minutes. Click “Zweryfikuj konto” again and the bot sends a new one.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>The page asks me to go back to my previous browser</summary>
        <p>The whole sign-in has to happen in one browser. Finish it where you opened the link. If you can't, click “Zweryfikuj konto” again and open the new link in the browser where you'll sign in to Riot.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I don't play on EUNE</summary>
        <p>You can link an account from EUNE, EUW or NA. Other regions aren't supported yet.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I want to link a different Riot account</summary>
        <p>Remove the current link in “Moje konto” first, then verify the new account. One Riot account can be linked to only one Discord account.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>My rank on Discord is wrong</summary>
        <p>The bot shows the rank from the last refresh. Click “Odśwież rangę” in “Moje konto” and give it a moment.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens if I leave the Discord server?</summary>
        <p>The link stays, and the bot restores your roles when you come back. If you want it removed and you're no longer on the server, email <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
